# Dogfood battery receipts

This directory holds the immutable receipts produced by the
previous-release PipelineK dogfood battery defined in
`docs/v2/05-roadmap/CI_TEST_RELEASE_WORKFLOW.md` §6.

**Authoritative schema:**
`docs/v2/05-roadmap/CI_TEST_RELEASE_WORKFLOW.md` §6.4 (mandatory
report fields) and §6.5 (promotion rules). A run without
`old_release`, `candidate_release`, every executed
`scenarios[…].outcome`, and an explicit `next_action` is **NOT a
report**; it is a log line.

**Filename pattern (per §6.6):**
`<yyyymm>/<sha>-<old-version>-vs-<candidate-version>.yaml`.

**Current state:**

- This directory exists so that the doc's prescribed path resolves.
- No receipts have been produced yet. The previous-release dogfood
  battery is **PLANNED**, not PASS.
- The v0.39.0 reference evidence lives in
  `docs/v2/07-uat/LPR_GATE_1_LOCAL_PRODUCTION_READY_0.39.0.md`
  (and related receipts at `docs/v2/07-uat/lfc-2e2-utilities/`).
  Those are `HISTORICAL_RELEASED_ARTIFACT`, not dogfood-battery
  receipts, and they do not satisfy §6 by themselves.

Do not drop raw logs or arbitrary YAML here. A file in this
directory must conform to §6.4 and §6.5 and must declare the binary
SHA-256s and the scenario catalogue it claims to cover.
